WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:13.062
The caravan entered Istanbul.

2
00:00:13.063 --> 00:00:15.243
The streets were crowded.

3
00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:20.794
Most men wore hats that were shaped like an upside-down flower pot.

4
00:00:20.795 --> 00:00:24.643
Each hat had a silk tail on top of it.

5
00:00:24.644 --> 00:00:30.376
Women wore long coats, and some covered their faces with a cloth.

6
00:00:30.377 --> 00:00:36.379
As the caravan passed by, people on the street called out to the travelers.

7
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.417
"What goods have you brought this time?"

8
00:00:39.418 --> 00:00:42.684
"Do you have any Chinese silk?"

9
00:00:42.685 --> 00:00:47.821
"Come to the Grand Bazaar!" shouted someone from the caravan.

10
00:00:47.822 --> 00:00:51.072
"Then you can see what we have!"

11
00:00:51.073 --> 00:00:55.410
The caravan stopped in front of a beautiful building.

12
00:00:55.411 --> 00:01:00.814
Through the main doorway, Mandy could see stalls and shops.

13
00:01:00.815 --> 00:01:04.279
They were filled with colorful items.

14
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.831
People from the caravan were unloading things to sell.

15
00:01:08.832 --> 00:01:14.275
"Wow! I'd like to shop here!" exclaimed Mandy.

16
00:01:14.276 --> 00:01:19.274
"What's that in your hand?" asked Vinnie.

17
00:01:19.275 --> 00:01:23.069
Mandy held up a pair of diamond earrings.

18
00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:29.478
"I forgot—Mom asked me to put these in her drawer!" she cried.

19
00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:33.826
"You'd better not lose them," warned Vinnie.

20
00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:37.485
"She'll be really upset."

21
00:01:37.486 --> 00:01:41.418
Mandy shrugged and put them in her pocket.

22
00:01:41.419 --> 00:01:44.739
"They're not real diamonds anyway."

23
00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:50.276
"How do we get off this animal?" said Vinnie, looking down.

24
00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:53.008
The camel stood quietly.

25
00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:57.090
"Maybe we can jump," suggested Mandy.

26
00:01:57.091 --> 00:02:03.267
"If you jump, you will break your leg or your neck," a man's voice said from below.

27
00:02:03.268 --> 00:02:07.561
Vinnie and Mandy saw a man staring at them.

28
00:02:07.562 --> 00:02:09.263
"How did you get up there?"

29
00:02:09.264 --> 00:02:12.499
the man asked, petting the camel.

30
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.760
"Kiraz the camel was not carrying any people earlier."

31
00:02:16.761 --> 00:02:22.738
"Uh, well, we …" Vinnie tried to explain.

32
00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:27.843
The man spoke to the camel and Kiraz knelt down.

33
00:02:27.844 --> 00:02:30.934
The children climbed off his back.

34
00:02:30.935 --> 00:02:34.274
"Thank you, sir," said Mandy.

35
00:02:34.275 --> 00:02:37.408
"Who are you?" the man asked.

36
00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:40.541
The children introduced themselves.

37
00:02:40.542 --> 00:02:43.667
"I am Ali," said the man.

38
00:02:43.668 --> 00:02:46.801
"I sell carpets and other things."

39
00:02:46.802 --> 00:02:51.368
The camel opened his mouth and stuck out a gray tongue.

40
00:02:51.369 --> 00:02:56.603
"I think Kiraz likes you!" laughed Ali.

41
00:02:56.604 --> 00:03:02.347
Vinnie and Mandy helped Ali carry rolls of carpets into the building.

42
00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:07.270
"The Grand Bazaar is the biggest market in the world," Ali explained.

43
00:03:07.271 --> 00:03:11.266
"It is one of the best places to buy and sell."

44
00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:14.412
"It's amazing," Mandy remarked.

45
00:03:14.413 --> 00:03:17.349
"It looks like the mall!"

46
00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:22.135
Many shops lined each side of the long building.

47
00:03:22.136 --> 00:03:26.573
People strolled down the middle, looking and buying.

48
00:03:26.574 --> 00:03:29.944
Ali stopped in front of one shop.

49
00:03:29.945 --> 00:03:33.227
A woman and a boy were already there.

50
00:03:33.228 --> 00:03:38.287
They were setting out beautiful pieces of jewelry and dishes.

51
00:03:38.288 --> 00:03:41.477
"This is my family," Ali said.

52
00:03:41.478 --> 00:03:45.279
"As you see, we sell many things, including carpets!"

53
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.371
He turned to his son.

54
00:03:47.372 --> 00:03:50.272
"Berk, take this bag to the coffee shop.

55
00:03:50.273 --> 00:03:53.468
Ask Hasad the owner to exchange it for silver."

56
00:03:53.469 --> 00:03:55.747
The boy nodded.

57
00:03:55.748 --> 00:03:59.017
"Can we go too?" asked Vinnie.

58
00:03:59.018 --> 00:04:01.747
Berk looked at his father.

59
00:04:01.748 --> 00:04:06.900
"Sure! The coffee shop is always fun to visit," Ali said.

60
00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:13.570
"But don't stay too long."
